# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets and stale
# build output from ever entering an image layer.

# Secrets. `.env.local` holds ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in local dev; on Fly every one of
# these arrives via `fly secrets set`, never baked in. A key in a layer survives
# `docker rm` and is readable by anyone who can pull the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/env

# Rust. The image deliberately builds no Rust — web/src/wasm/ is committed. This
# is the single largest thing in the tree and none of it is needed.
target/
crates/

# Dependencies and build output: reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
# Copying a host node_modules is how a macOS binary ends up in a Linux image.
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
deploy/dist-server/
web/.dev-plans/

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.github/
.githooks/

# Test, gate and audit apparatus. None of it runs in the image; the battery runs
# before the deploy, not inside it.
scripts/
bench/
reports/
docs/
research/
samples/
out/
graphify-out/
**/*.test.mjs
supabase/tests/

# Local noise.
.DS_Store
*.png
*.log
.claude/
